# system/_template/.canon-overrides — tracked backlog of canon class overrides.
#
# One "<page>|<class>" per line. A page listed here redefines a class that
# nl-brand.css already defines; because a page's <style> loads after the
# stylesheet, the local rule silently wins and the page stops tracking the
# design system while still appearing to use it.
#
# This file exists so `--strict` can fail on NEW overrides while a known
# backlog is worked down. Like .lint-waivers, a line here is a promise to come
# back, not a fix.
#
# Seeded 15/08/2026 with the 153 overrides present when the check was first
# built. CONSOLIDATION.md listed this rule under "Future-proofing" in July and
# it was never implemented; these 153 are what accumulated in the meantime.
#
# To clear a line: either use the canon class as-is, or rename yours to a
# page-specific prefix (.est-row, .mr-cpill) so it cannot collide. Deleting the
# line is the last step, not the first.
